      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Before settlers arrived, the Adena Culture built burial mounds here, leaving earthwork structures that hint at a 3,000‑year‑old civilization.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.pa.gov/agencies/dcnr/recreation/where-to-go/state-parks/find-a-park/pymatuning-state-park/history",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "In 1935, the Civilian Conservation Corps built Camp NP‑11‑PA at Pymatuning, a historic structure that guarded the area during World War II.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
